# Tailwind CSS Development Standards

## Objective
Establish consistent styling patterns using Tailwind CSS that promote maintainable, responsive, and accessible designs in the Downlodr application.

## Context
- Tailwind CSS 3.4+ with custom design tokens
- Dark mode support with class-based strategy
- Custom color palette for brand consistency
- Responsive design for desktop application
- Component-based styling approach

## Rules

### Design System Usage

#### Color Palette
- **Use design tokens**: Prefer custom colors over default Tailwind colors
- **Semantic naming**: Use colors that convey meaning and purpose
- **Dark mode support**: Always provide dark mode variants
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="bg-primary text-white dark:bg-darkMode dark:text-darkModeLight"
  ✅ className="border-divider dark:border-darkModeBorderColor"
  ✅ className="text-availableStatus dark:text-darkModeNotAvailableStatus"
  
  ❌ className="bg-red-500 text-white" // Use semantic colors
  ❌ className="bg-blue-600" // Use custom design tokens
  ```

#### Typography
- **Consistent text sizes**: Use standard Tailwind text utilities
- **Font weights**: Limit to established weights (normal, medium, semibold)
- **Line heights**: Use appropriate line heights for readability
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="text-sm font-medium leading-5"
  ✅ className="text-lg font-semibold"
  ✅ className="text-xs text-darkModeLight dark:text-darkModeLight"
  
  ❌ className="text-[13px]" // Use standard sizes
  ❌ className="font-[550]" // Use standard weights
  ```

#### Spacing
- **Consistent spacing scale**: Use Tailwind's spacing scale
- **Logical spacing**: Group related elements with appropriate spacing
- **Component padding**: Use consistent padding patterns
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="p-4 space-y-2"
  ✅ className="mx-2 my-4"
  ✅ className="gap-4 grid grid-cols-1"
  
  ❌ className="p-[15px]" // Use scale values
  ❌ className="ml-[13px]" // Arbitrary values
  ```

### Layout Patterns

#### Flexbox Layouts
- **Flex containers**: Use flex for one-dimensional layouts
- **Alignment utilities**: Use semantic alignment classes
- **Responsive behavior**: Consider how layouts adapt
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"
  ✅ className="flex flex-col space-y-4"
  ✅ className="flex flex-wrap items-start"
  
  ❌ className="flex justify-center items-center gap-1 gap-2" // Conflicting gaps
  ```

#### Grid Layouts
- **Grid for two-dimensional layouts**: Use grid for complex layouts
- **Responsive grids**: Use responsive grid patterns
- **Grid alignment**: Proper use of grid alignment utilities
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4"
  ✅ className="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr] items-center"
  ✅ className="grid place-items-center min-h-screen"
  
  ❌ className="grid grid-cols-1 grid-cols-2" // Conflicting values
  ```

### Component Styling

#### Button Variants
- **Consistent button patterns**: Use established button variants
- **State variants**: Include hover, focus, and disabled states
- **Size variants**: Use consistent sizing patterns
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 disabled:opacity-50 px-4 py-2 rounded-md"
  ✅ className="border border-componentBorder hover:bg-lightGray dark:border-darkModeBorderColor"
  ✅ className="h-7 px-4 text-sm" // Small button
  
  ❌ className="bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600" // Use design tokens
  ```

#### Modal and Dialog Styling
- **Consistent modal patterns**: Use established modal styling
- **Backdrop styling**: Consistent overlay styling
- **Modal sizing**: Use responsive modal sizes
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="fixed inset-0 bg-black/50 flex items-center justify-center"
  ✅ className="bg-body dark:bg-darkMode rounded-lg shadow-lg max-w-md w-full m-4"
  ✅ className="p-6 space-y-4"
  
  ❌ className="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-full" // Use inset utilities
  ```

#### Form Elements
- **Input styling**: Consistent input field styling
- **Form layout**: Proper form element spacing
- **Validation states**: Include error and success states
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="border border-border dark:border-darkModeBorderColor rounded-md px-3 py-2"
  ✅ className="focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary focus:border-primary"
  ✅ className="border-red-500 text-red-500" // Error state
  
  ❌ className="border-gray-300" // Use design tokens
  ```

### Responsive Design

#### Breakpoint Usage
- **Desktop-first approach**: Design for desktop, adapt for smaller screens
- **Logical breakpoints**: Use breakpoints that make sense for content
- **Consistent breakpoint usage**: Use established breakpoints
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="grid grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-1"
  ✅ className="text-lg md:text-base sm:text-sm"
  ✅ className="px-6 md:px-4 sm:px-2"
  
  ❌ className="lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-3" // Unnecessary duplication
  ```

#### Content Adaptation
- **Text scaling**: Appropriate text sizes for different screens
- **Spacing adaptation**: Adjust spacing for different screen sizes
- **Component visibility**: Show/hide elements appropriately
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="hidden md:block" // Hide on mobile
  ✅ className="block md:hidden" // Show only on mobile
  ✅ className="p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8" // Progressive spacing
  ```

### Dark Mode Implementation

#### Color Switching
- **Consistent dark mode patterns**: Use established dark mode colors
- **Complete coverage**: Ensure all elements have dark mode variants
- **Readable contrast**: Maintain good contrast ratios
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="bg-body dark:bg-darkMode text-gray-900 dark:text-darkModeLight"
  ✅ className="border-border dark:border-darkModeBorderColor"
  ✅ className="hover:bg-lightGray dark:hover:bg-darkModeHover"
  
  ❌ className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800" // Use design tokens
  ```

#### Component Adaptation
- **State-aware styling**: Dark mode variants for all interactive states
- **Icon and media adaptation**: Ensure icons work in both modes
- **Focus states**: Maintain visibility in both modes
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="focus:ring-primary dark:focus:ring-primary"
  ✅ className="bg-inputDarkMode dark:bg-inputDarkMode border-inputDarkModeBorder"
  ```

### Performance Optimization

#### Class Organization
- **Logical grouping**: Group related utilities together
- **Avoid duplication**: Don't repeat the same utility
- **Use component variants**: Extract common patterns
  ```tsx
  ✅ // Grouped by concern
  className="
    flex items-center justify-between
    bg-body dark:bg-darkMode
    border border-border dark:border-darkModeBorderColor
    p-4 rounded-lg
  "
  
  ❌ className="flex bg-body flex items-center border" // Poor organization
  ```

#### Utility Composition
- **Compose utilities**: Build complex styles from simple utilities
- **Component extraction**: Extract frequently used patterns
- **Conditional classes**: Use conditional class application properly
  ```tsx
  ✅ const buttonClasses = cn(
    "px-4 py-2 rounded-md font-medium transition-colors",
    variant === 'primary' && "bg-primary text-white hover:bg-primary/90",
    variant === 'secondary' && "border border-border bg-transparent",
    disabled && "opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed"
  );
  
  ❌ // Inline conditional styling
  className={`px-4 py-2 ${variant === 'primary' ? 'bg-blue-500' : 'bg-gray-200'}`}
  ```

### Accessibility

#### Focus States
- **Visible focus indicators**: Ensure focus states are visible
- **Consistent focus styling**: Use consistent focus patterns
- **Keyboard navigation**: Support keyboard navigation
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary focus:ring-offset-2"
  ✅ className="focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary"
  
  ❌ className="focus:outline-none" // Without alternative focus indicator
  ```

#### Color Contrast
- **Sufficient contrast**: Ensure adequate color contrast
- **Text readability**: Maintain readable text in all states
- **Interactive element clarity**: Make interactive elements obvious
  ```tsx
  ✅ className="text-gray-900 dark:text-darkModeLight"
  ✅ className="bg-availableStatus text-white" // High contrast
  
  ❌ className="text-gray-400 bg-gray-300" // Poor contrast
  ```

## Exceptions
- **Third-party component styling**: May require custom CSS
- **Complex animations**: May need custom CSS or CSS-in-JS
- **Legacy component migration**: Gradual migration acceptable
- **Performance-critical sections**: May require optimized approaches

## Enforcement
- Tailwind CSS IntelliSense for IDE support
- ESLint plugin for Tailwind CSS
- Prettier plugin for class sorting
- Design system documentation and examples

